# ORICAL V3 Roadmap

## Version Lineage
- V1: Daily Summary
- V2: Orical (Python/Tkinter)
- V3: Full production app (Mac-first)

## V3 Goal
Build Orical into a stable, modular command center app that feels native on macOS, supports long-term growth, and can later expand to other platforms.

## Primary Product Pillars
1. Daily Intelligence
- Unified feed for world news, local context, market signals, and "On This Day" history.
- Fast summaries with source links.

2. System Awareness
- Live RAM, storage, Wi-Fi bars and status.
- Background refresh with resilient fallbacks.

3. Radio
- Global station search, presets, favorites, instant play.
- Recover playback state on relaunch.

4. AI Operator
- Text-first command bar to run actions across modules.
- Examples: "summarize today", "play preset 3", "show system risk", "build daily brief".

5. Mission Control UX
- Fast startup, clear navigation, and reliable background behavior.

## Technical Direction (Recommended)
Mac-first native rewrite:
- UI: SwiftUI (+ AppKit bridge only where needed)
- Storage: SwiftData (SQLite under the hood)
- Networking: URLSession + structured async tasks
- Audio: AVFoundation
- Maps/Globe: MapKit globe mode + custom overlays
- AI: OpenAI API integration through a service layer
- Logging/Telemetry: Unified logger with local rolling logs

Why this direction:
- Native permissions and startup behavior are cleaner than Tkinter.
- Better performance and packaging for a real desktop app.
- Easier long-term maintenance than a single-file Python GUI.

