## 4-Phase Delivery Plan
## Phase 0: Foundation (Week 1-2)
Deliverables:
- Xcode project scaffold with module boundaries.
- Navigation shell and theme tokens.
- Data model and repository interfaces.
- Local persistence wired (settings, presets, cache).

Exit criteria:
- App launches in <2s on a normal Mac.
- Navigation and persistence are stable.

## Phase 1: Core Feature Parity (Week 3-6)
Deliverables:
- System panel (RAM/storage/Wi-Fi with bars).
- Radio presets/favorites/search/playback.
- Daily feed ingestion + normalized article model.
- Baseline dashboard cards.

Exit criteria:
- All V2 core features available in V3.
- No hard crash in 24h soak test.

## Phase 2: Intelligence Layer (Week 7-10)
Deliverables:
- "On This Day" historical timeline section.
- Assistant command bar with action dispatch.
- Daily briefing generator (structured sections).
- Confidence/risk scoring for signals.

Exit criteria:
- User can run end-to-end workflow from one command.
- Briefing quality and reliability acceptable for daily use.

## Phase 3: Productionization (Week 11-14)
Deliverables:
- Error handling, retry, offline degradation paths.
- Telemetry/log viewer and diagnostics bundle.
- Packaging/signing/notarization preparation.
- Regression test suite and release checklist.

Exit criteria:
- Beta-ready build shared with migration path from V2.

## V2 to V3 Migration Plan
Data to migrate:
- `settings.json` values
- Radio favorites/presets
- Cached note/history items (if retained)

Migration strategy:
1. On first launch, detect V2 data files.
2. Run one-time importer into V3 models.
3. Write migration report to local logs.
4. Keep original files untouched for rollback.

## Quality Gates
- Crash-free session target: >99%
- UI response target: key interactions <100ms perceived latency
- Feed refresh target: complete within 5-10s on normal connection
- Test coverage target: critical paths fully covered

## Known Risks and Mitigations
1. API instability / rate limits
- Mitigation: caching, backoff, and fallback providers.

2. Background task reliability
- Mitigation: central scheduler and observable job states.

3. Scope creep
- Mitigation: strict phase gates and versioned feature flags.

## V3.0 Scope Lock (What ships first)
- Dashboard, System, Radio, Timeline, Assistant command bar, Settings.

Not in V3.0:
- Cross-platform desktop/mobile ports.
- Voice control (defer until native permissions + UX are production-ready).

## Immediate Sprint (Next 7 Days)
1. Create `OricalV3` Xcode project and module folders.
2. Implement app shell, routing, and theme system.
3. Port System Status module first (small and measurable).
4. Port Radio module second (presets + playback + favorites).
5. Stand up integration service interfaces (news/markets/weather/AI stubs).

## Success Definition for V3 Launch
- Replaces V2 for daily personal use.
- Stable startup and background refresh behavior.
- Clear upgrade path and maintainable codebase.
